{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>for all, and the governors</b> — corresponding to the fathers of Israel, who are the twelve tribes. Only ninety-six, seventy-seven, according to your ability — there is no reason for them. <i>Parim</i> and <i>tzipirim</i> in feminine language, and the opposite of this is <i>nashim pilagshim</i> in masculine language." "<b>and they bore the people</b> — like the sense of <i>יִנְשָׂאֻהוּ אַנְשֵׁי מְקֹמוֹ</i> [the men of his place shall bear him], and its meaning has already been explained."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:20.325893064Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}